    <string name="settings_harman_fullscreen_experimental_description">Let CarPlay occupy the OEM side-panel area on supported Harman head units. Applies when the CarPlay window next opens; other firmware may display incorrectly.</string>
    <string name="settings_carplay_same_task">Keep CarPlay in the launcher card (experimental)</string>
    <string name="settings_carplay_same_task_description">For launchers that show DiPlay in a card or picture-in-picture window, such as BYD\'s DiYou desktop. CarPlay opens in DiPlay\'s own window, as in 0.2.11 and earlier, instead of a separate full-screen one. Applies the next time CarPlay opens, without disconnecting.</string>
    <string name="settings_hotspot_name_non_english">Names with Chinese or other non-English characters can leave CarPlay on “Getting CarPlay ready…”: some head units broadcast them in a form the iPhone doesn’t find. If that happens, rename the car hotspot with English letters and digits.</string>
    <string name="settings_speech_without_low_rates">Clearer navigation voice over USB (experimental)</string>
    <string name="settings_speech_without_low_rates_description">Over USB the iPhone can send navigation prompts and Siri’s spoken replies as 8 kHz phone-quality audio. This stops offering 8 and 16 kHz for that audio so the iPhone picks a higher rate. If prompts go silent, turn it off. Reconnects CarPlay.</string>
    <string name="settings_call_at_call_rate">Calls at the call\'s own rate (experimental)</string>
    <string name="settings_call_at_call_rate_description">Offer calls as PCM at the call\'s own rate (8, 16, 24 or 32 kHz) instead of 48 kHz Opus, as the stock CarPlay receiver does. Takes effect at the next connection. If a call has no sound, turn this off.</string>
    <string name="bluetooth_connections_not_real">This head unit’s Android Bluetooth reports a connection, but nothing reaches the iPhone: even a connection to a service that does not exist succeeds. Bluetooth here is handled by the maker’s own module, which apps cannot use, so wireless CarPlay cannot work on this head unit. Try a USB connection.</string>
    <string name="bluetooth_cannot_open_connections">This head unit’s Android Bluetooth cannot open connections for apps: its firmware leaves out the part that apps connect through. Calls and music over the car’s own Bluetooth are not affected, but wireless CarPlay cannot work on this head unit. Try a USB connection.</string>
    <string name="bluetooth_will_not_stay_on_hint">If Bluetooth will not stay on there, this head unit keeps Bluetooth for its own calls and music, and apps cannot use it. Wireless CarPlay cannot work in that case: use a USB cable.</string>
